
Rem_METHODS
The photographs under the optical microscope were made in a microscope Nikon model Optiphot and those under S.E.M. in a microscope ISI model SX-25.
titre$ KEY TO MEMBERS OF THE DOMESTICUS GROUP
1,0$ remarque : According to Dr. Roger Kemp (personal communication), cultural problems exist in this group as all species are homothallic without clamp connections./// However, most of them produce oidia which may be used for homing and lethal reaction studies.

1,0 $ Veil cells monomorphic, consisting of globosse, ovoid or broadly ellipsoid,thin walled, hyalin cells $ Micaceus group

1,2 $ Veil cells dimorphic, consisting of the above mentioned cells and of cylindric, elongate, pyriform or else swollen cells which are mostly pale to distinctly brown and not to distinctly encrusted . 2 Domesticus group 2(1).-

2,0$ Spores large and dark-coloured (spore print blackish), 11-16 x 6.5-9.5 µm,with distinctly eccentric germ pore $ C. flocculosus DC.: Fr.

2,3 $ Spores smaller and mostly paler, with ± central germ pore, spore print in mass dark chocolate brown with purplish tint 
3,0$(2).- Spores 8.5-10.5 x 4.5-5.2 µm, ellipsoid to ovate, ocassionally slightly phaseoliform in side view, veil coherent, thick and patch-like $ C. bipellis Romagn.

3,4 $ Not as above; spores either not exceeding 5 µm width and then often phaseoliform in side view, or more than 5.2 µm broad; veil more floccose atleast on expanded cap 

4 ,5$(3).- Spores not exceeding 5 µm in width, often phaseoliform in side view,cheilocystidia broadly ellipsoid 

4,6 $ Spores exceeding (5)5.2 µm in width, rarely phaseoliform in side view,cheilocystidia mostly lageniform (with intermixed ellipsoid or subglobosecystidia) 
5,0 $(4).- Spores 7-10 x 4-5 µm, stem base with or without a volva-like zone $ C. domesticus (Bolt.) Gray
5,0 $ Spores somewhat shorter and narrower, 6.5-8.5(9) x 3-4.5(5)µm, stem base always (?) with volva-like veil zone (see our remarks under C. domesticus) $ C. ellisii P.D. Orton

6,0 $ Spores predominantly ovoid to broadly ellipsoid, 7, 3-9 x 4.6-5, 8 µm,brown-coloured veil elements mostly slender, ± cylindric to moderatelyexpanded $ C. xanthothrix Romagn.
6,0 $ Spores predominantly ellipsoid to ovoid, 8, 5-11 (12.5) x 5-6,3 µm,brown-coloured veil elements (particulary end cells) mostly broader, oftendistinctly expanded, broadly conical, pyriform, vesiculose $ C. radians (Desm.) Fr.
